# Overview

We used [GATK v4.2.0.0](https://gatk.broadinstitute.org/hc/en-us/sections/360012354372-4-2-0-0) ([DePristo et al., 2011](https://www.nature.com/articles/ng.806)) for SNP calling in the two *Arabis alpina* populations.  
Read groups were assigned, adapters were soft-clipped, duplicates were marked, and reads were aligned to the Pajares reference genome [v5.1](http://www.arabis-alpina.org/data/ArabisAlpina/assemblies/V5.1/Arabis_alpina.MPIPZ.version_5.1.chr.all.fasta.gz) ([Jiao & Schneeberger, 2017](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1369526616301315?via%3Dihub)) using the MEM algorithm of **BWA v0.7.17** ([Li & Durbin, 2009](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19451168/)).  
Additionally, we applied hard filters.


# Reduced genotyping of outcrossers

#!/bin/bash
set -euo pipefail

ref="/netscratch/dep_coupland/grp_fulgione/bastiaan/data/reference/Alpina_V5.1/Arabis_alpina.MPIPZ.version_5.1.chr.all.fasta"
positions="positions.txt"

# positions.txt: chrom<TAB>pos
awk '{print $1"\t"$2-1"\t"$2}' "$positions" > positions.bed

bcftools mpileup \
    -f "$ref" \
    -q 30 \
    -R positions.bed \
    -Ou \
    *_gatk42_bwamem.sorted.bam | \
bcftools call \
    -mv \
    -Oz \
    -o mpileup_positions.vcf.gz

bcftools index mpileup_positions.vcf.gz



<br>

# Pipeline

## fastqtosam_all.sh
Convert FASTQ files to unmapped SAM files and assign read groups from header information  
(valid for DNBseq headers 2020).

<br>

## markadapters_all.sh and discount_all.sh
*Note: Adapters were already removed by the sequencing provider (BGI).*  
Scripts to mark adapters and soft-clip them, supplied with 5′ and 3′ adapter sequences from DNBseq.

<br>

## bwamem_all.sh
Map samples to the *A. alpina* Pajares reference genome.

<br>

## mergebamalignment_all.sh and sortmabam_all.sh
Merge mapped BAM files and raw unmapped SAM files, then sort the merged BAM file.

<br>

## markduplicates.sh
Mark PCR duplicates (reads derived from the same DNA fragment).

<br>

## haplocallergvcf_all2.sh
Per-sample genotyping using GATK HaplotypeCaller with `--output-mode EMIT_ALL_ACTIVE_SITES`  
to emit an all-sites VCF (including invariant sites).  
Outputs raw genotype calls in GVCF format.

<br>

## gDBimport_Alpina_Genomes.sh
Create a GATK GenomicsDB database from individual GVCFs.

<br>

## genotypeGVCF_Alpina_Genomes.sh
Perform joint genotyping for all samples using the GenomicsDB.

<br>

## run_FilterVCF_Alpina_Genomes.sh
Filter variants with custom scripts per genotype and per site:  
- Genotype quality ≥ 30  
- Depth ≥ 5  
- Minimum genome-wide coverage ≥ 10×  
- Biallelic SNPs only
